# round 115 (w132): the learned enzyme allocation under the GECKO pool, with an objective that pushes the pool to bind. Round 19 (w32_lpelpoolbio100) projected the abundance head onto the pool by construction and measured the projection never engaging (factor 1 on every batch): the head never asked for the whole budget. --flux-pool-fill-weight adds, outside the constraint ramp, the shortfall of the head protein mass below the pool, so the head must spend it and can only choose where. Two readouts, three seeds each, everything else as round 19 (elastic program, capacity scale 100, no proteome): the forced growth column (biomass readout) against w32_lpelpoolbio100 (0.704, 0.743, 0.670) and w32_lpelbio100, and the gated readout against w32_lpelgate100 (0.816, 0.810, 0.783). Read fixed here: paired by seed; the cell also logs feas_pool_scale_mean and feas_pool_fill_shortfall, which say whether the pool now binds.
TC_LP_WORKERS=8 ESS_ARM=flux_projection_anchored_nodiss ESS_HIDDEN=12 ESS_HEADS=4 ESS_LAYERS=1 ESS_PREPROC=1 ESS_EPOCHS=200 ESS_BATCH=32 ESS_POSW=1 ESS_LR=1e-3 ESS_SPLIT=ess_fcl_val0.2_s0.json.gz ESS_SEED=2701 ESS_TAG=_w132lpelpoolfillgate100 ESS_OUT=w132_lpelpoolfillgate100_h12l1p1_e200_s2701 ESS_EXTRA='--kcat-tier predicted --thermo-source union_external --constraint-warmup-epochs 20 --constraint-scale 0 --conc-upper-m 1.0 --apply-media dataset --flux-parameterization lp --flux-lp-slack-penalty 1.0 --flux-capacity-scale 100 --flux-pool-by-construction --flux-pool-fill-weight 1.0 --ess-readout gated'
